prompt:
You are a compliance referee. Explain this cross-department gap to a launch manager in 2-3 plain sentences and give 2-3 concrete fix options. Use ONLY these facts; do not invent any.
Seam type: data_residency_breach
Title: 2 supplier(s) process customer data outside UK/EEA, against the customer terms
Departments: Finance, Legal, Product
Facts: {"allowed_regions": ["UK", "EEA"], "breaches": ["V007 VerifyPoint Inc: customer identity data processed in US-East (United States); C-2026-045 DPA signed=True", "V003 Harbor Analytics Inc: customer payment data processed in US-East (United States); C-2025-020 DPA signed=False"], "promise": "Customer payment data is processed and stored only within the UK or EEA, including by sub-processors."}
Return JSON: {"explanation": str, "fix_options": [str]}

response:
```json
{
  "explanation": "Our customer terms promise that customer payment data is processed and stored only within the UK or EEA, including by sub-processors, but two suppliers process customer data in US-East (United States). V003 Harbor Analytics Inc processes customer payment data there, which directly breaks the promise, and it has no signed DPA under contract C-2025-020. V007 VerifyPoint Inc processes customer identity data there and does have a signed DPA (C-2026-045), but a DPA does not change where the data is processed, so this still falls outside the allowed UK/EEA regions.",
  "fix_options": [
    "Require both suppliers to move processing of our customer data into the UK or EEA before launch. Product and Legal confirm the change in writing, and Finance handles any resulting contract or cost changes.",
    "Replace V003 Harbor Analytics Inc first, since it handles payment data with no signed DPA. Use a supplier that processes in the UK/EEA, then do the same for V007 VerifyPoint Inc if it cannot relocate.",
    "If moving or replacing a supplier is not possible before launch, have Legal decide whether to revise the customer terms. Legal would also need to confirm whether identity data is covered by the current promise and put a signed DPA in place for V003 under C-2025-020."
  ]
}
```
